# 📘 BLUEPRINT: Nifty RSI-Based Intraday Options Selling Algo
> **Version:** 2.2  
> **Language:** Node.js  
> **Broker:** Angel One SmartAPI  
> **Exchange:** NSE (National Stock Exchange of India)  
> **Instrument:** NIFTY 50 Options (Near Expiry / Monthly fallback)  

---

## 🧠 Strategy Overview

This is an **intraday options selling strategy** that runs **every NSE trading day** (not just expiry day).

The algo watches **Nifty Spot RSI (14-period, on 5-minute candles)** and initiates directional short option trades when RSI reaches extreme overbought or oversold levels.

---

### 📐 RSI Signal Logic

| RSI Condition | Action |
|---|---|
| RSI **≥ 80** (Overbought) | **Sell an OTM CALL** + Buy a hedge CALL further OTM |
| RSI **≤ 20** (Oversold) | **Sell an OTM PUT** + Buy a hedge PUT further OTM |

- **Only one trade per day.** Once a signal fires and positions are placed, RSI monitoring stops for the day.
- RSI is checked **every 1 minute** (on the latest completed 5-min candle close) until entry.
- If no RSI signal fires before **3:00 PM IST** → algo exits gracefully with no trades.

---

### 🎯 Strike Selection — Selling Leg

- On **RSI ≥ 80 (CALL sell):**
  - Fetch live option chain.
  - Find the **first OTM CALL** strike above current Nifty spot (rounded to nearest 50-point interval).
  - Prefer a strike that is **1–2 strikes OTM** (i.e., 50–100 points above spot).
  - Check **Open Interest (OI) and volume** for liquidity — minimum thresholds defined in `config.js`.

- On **RSI ≤ 20 (PUT sell):**
  - Fetch live option chain.
  - Find the **first OTM PUT** strike below current Nifty spot (rounded to nearest 50-point interval).
  - Prefer a strike that is **1–2 strikes OTM** (i.e., 50–100 points below spot).
  - Check **OI and volume** for liquidity — minimum thresholds defined in `config.js`.

---

### 🛡️ Hedge (Buying Leg)

After selecting the sell strike:
1. Note the **LTP (Last Traded Price)** of the sold option = `sellPremium`.
2. Target hedge premium = `sellPremium / 2` (half of what was collected).
3. Scan the option chain **further OTM** (in the same direction: higher CALL strikes / lower PUT strikes) for the strike whose **LTP is closest to `sellPremium / 2`**.
4. Also verify liquidity (OI + volume) on the hedge leg.
5. **BUY** that hedge strike.

This forms a **vertical spread** (Bull Put Spread or Bear Call Spread) with the hedge costing approximately half the premium collected, giving a defined-risk structure.

---

### 📅 Expiry Selection Logic

The algo sells options on the **nearest upcoming expiry**, with one exception:

| Scenario | Expiry to Use |
|---|---|
| **Normal week** (not last week of month) | **Current week's weekly expiry** (Thursday) |
| **Last week of the month** (Thursday expiry = monthly expiry, or within 3 trading days of monthly expiry) | **Monthly expiry only** — do NOT use the weekly; it IS the monthly |
| Thursday is an NSE holiday | Roll to the **preceding trading day** (Wednesday, or Tuesday if Wednesday is also a holiday) |

**"Last week of the month" detection:**
- Get the monthly expiry date (last Thursday of the month).
- If today's date is within 3 calendar days of the monthly expiry → treat this week as "monthly expiry week."
- In that case, `getExpiryDate()` returns the monthly expiry date directly.

> ⚠️ **Note on Nifty expiry day change:** Nifty weekly expiry moved from **Thursday to Monday** effective **April 4, 2025**. Verify the current expiry day with NSE before deployment and update `config.js` accordingly. The blueprint uses Monday as the current weekly expiry day below — adjust if needed.

---

### 🚪 Exit Rule

Once the spread is live, a **P&L monitor** (`pnlMonitor.js`) runs every 1 minute and checks the current mark-to-market P&L of the combined spread position. Exits are triggered as follows:

| Condition | Action |
|---|---|
| **Net P&L ≥ +1% of margin used** | 🟢 **Take Profit** — exit both legs immediately via MARKET order |
| **Net P&L ≤ −2% of margin used** | 🔴 **Stop Loss** — exit both legs immediately via MARKET order |
| **3:25 PM IST reached** (hard cutoff) | 🕒 **Force Exit** — exit ALL open legs regardless of P&L |

> **Why CARRYFORWARD instead of INTRADAY?** Intraday (MIS) orders are auto squared-off by the broker in the last 30 minutes of the session, which triggers at unpredictable times, attracts higher brokerage/penalty charges, and removes control from the algo. CARRYFORWARD (CNC/NRML) orders are never auto squared-off — the algo retains full control and manually exits everything at 3:25 PM via `exitManager.runForceExit()`. If the algo crashes and misses the 3:25 PM exit, the position simply carries overnight with no penalty — which is acceptable and recoverable.

**Margin used** = SPAN + Exposure margin blocked by the broker for the short leg of the spread. This value is captured at entry from SmartAPI's funds/margins API and stored in `positionTracker`.

**Mark-to-market P&L** is computed every minute as:
```
currentPnL = (sellLeg.entryPrice - sellLeg.currentLTP) × qty    // profit as premium decays
           + (hedgeLeg.currentLTP - hedgeLeg.entryPrice) × qty  // hedge leg gain/loss
```

- The P&L monitor **stops** as soon as either target or SL is hit and orders are placed.
- If neither is hit by 3:25 PM, `exitManager.js` takes over and force-exits everything.
- At 3:25 PM the exit is **all legs** — no ITM/OTM distinction — because this is a hard time cutoff, not an expiry settlement check.

