## 📊 Sample Trade Example

**Scenario:** RSI hits 82 at 10:15 AM. Nifty spot = 23,200.

| Leg | Strike | Type | Action | LTP at Entry | Lots | Qty |
|-----|--------|------|--------|--------------|------|-----|
| Sell CALL | 23,300 | CE | SELL | ₹85 | 2 | 50 |
| Buy CALL (hedge) | 23,500 | CE | BUY | ₹42 | 2 | 50 |

**Net premium collected:** (85 − 42) × 50 = **₹2,150**

**Margin used (SPAN + Exposure, fetched from RMS):** ₹45,000 *(example)*

**Profit target:** 1% of ₹45,000 = **₹450** → exit when spread P&L ≥ +₹450

**Stop loss:** 2% of ₹45,000 = **₹900** → exit when spread P&L ≤ −₹900

---

**How P&L is tracked (every 1 minute):**
```
currentPnL = (85 - sellLeg.currentLTP) × 50   ← sell leg gains as CALL premium falls
           + (hedgeLeg.currentLTP - 42) × 50   ← hedge leg gain/loss
```

---

**Exit Scenario A — Target Hit (normal case):**
- At 11:30 AM, Nifty pulls back. Sell CALL LTP drops to ₹68, hedge CALL LTP drops to ₹31.
- P&L = (85 − 68) × 50 + (31 − 42) × 50 = 850 − 550 = **+₹300** ← not yet
- At 12:15 PM, sell CALL LTP = ₹58, hedge CALL LTP = ₹27.
- P&L = (85 − 58) × 50 + (27 − 42) × 50 = 1350 − 750 = **+₹600** ✅ Target hit (≥ ₹450)
- → `pnlMonitor` fires exit. Both legs closed via MARKET order. Algo ends.

**Exit Scenario B — Stop Loss Hit:**
- At 10:45 AM, Nifty rallies sharply. Sell CALL LTP rises to ₹103, hedge CALL LTP = ₹56.
- P&L = (85 − 103) × 50 + (56 − 42) × 50 = −900 + 700 = **−₹200** ← not yet
- At 11:00 AM, sell CALL LTP = ₹118, hedge CALL LTP = ₹64.
- P&L = (85 − 118) × 50 + (64 − 42) × 50 = −1650 + 1100 = **−₹550** ← not yet
- At 11:15 AM, sell CALL LTP = ₹130, hedge CALL LTP = ₹70.
- P&L = (85 − 130) × 50 + (70 − 42) × 50 = −2250 + 1400 = **−₹850** ← not yet
- At 11:30 AM, sell CALL LTP = ₹135, hedge CALL LTP = ₹72.
- P&L = (85 − 135) × 50 + (72 − 42) × 50 = −2500 + 1500 = **−₹1,000** 🔴 SL hit (≤ −₹900)
- → `pnlMonitor` fires exit. Both legs closed via MARKET order. Algo ends.

**Exit Scenario C — 3:25 PM Force Exit (TP/SL never triggered):**
- P&L oscillates between −₹300 and +₹200 all day, never hitting TP or SL.
- At 3:25 PM, `exitManager.runForceExit()` is called.
- Both legs closed via MARKET order regardless of moneyness or P&L.
- Final P&L logged and algo ends.

